     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p6-information-block",
     "replacement": "To solve a quadratic equation in the form $ax^2+b=c$, where $a\\neq 0$:\n\n1. Isolate $x^2$.\n2. If the isolated value is negative, there is no real solution. Otherwise, square root both sides and include $\\pm$.",
